# Repo runtime: WSL + pnpm

This project lives in **WSL (Ubuntu)**, not Windows PowerShell.

## Shell

- Run all commands in WSL bash (`/home/ac/projects/hm_blog`).
- Do **not** use PowerShell, `cmd`, or Windows `npm`/`npx` against UNC paths.
- Prefer: `wsl -d Ubuntu-22.04 -e bash -lc 'cd /home/ac/projects/hm_blog && …'` when the agent host is Windows.

## Package manager

Use **pnpm** only (not npm/npx for project scripts):

| Intent | Command |
|--------|---------|
| Install | `pnpm install` |
| Dev server | `pnpm dev` |
| Build | `pnpm build` |
| Test (all) | `pnpm test` |
| Test one file | `pnpm exec vitest run src/utils/__tests__/pastEventArchive.test.js` |
| Add dep | `pnpm add <pkg>` |
| Add devDep | `pnpm add -D <pkg>` |

Do not use `pnpm dlx vitest` / a global Vitest for this repo — that can pull Vitest 5+ and break `jsdom` resolution. Always use the workspace Vitest via `pnpm test` or `pnpm exec vitest`.
